# 11. Final Project Objective

MAGNIKA is intended to develop a new materials-aware method for designing synchronous reluctance motors.

Its long-term ambition is to connect metallurgy, magnetic physics, electromagnetic FEM, motor topology and power-electronic control within one optimization framework.

The commercial objective is to develop high-performance, cost-effective PM-free motors that reduce reliance on rare-earth permanent magnets and provide a robust alternative for manufacturers and industries that value supply-chain independence.

**The central principle of MAGNIKA is that the motor, its magnetic material and its electrical excitation should be designed as one interconnected system.**